WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.613 --> 00:00:02.640
Have you ever wondered

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:06.560
if there are more natural ways
to lower your high blood pressure,

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.520
guard against Alzheimer's,
lose weight, and feel better?

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:12.720
Well, it turns out there is!

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:15.200
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.920
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:19.280
Today we try to
answer the question

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:23.520
do the benefits of Ozempic
outweigh the risks?

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:25.200
Even the drug manufacturers

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.200
of Ozempic
and similar weight-loss drugs

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:28.640
cop to the long list

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:30.880
of potentially serious
side effects.

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:32.880
The absolute risks, though,

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:34.720
for serious issues
like pancreatitis,

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:36.720
thyroid cancer,
bowel obstruction,

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:38.720
were all about 1% or less

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:41.760
per year
of using GLP-1-type drugs.

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:44.000
Of course, when millions
of people are on these drugs,

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:45.520
even relatively rare
side effects

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:47.920
will occur
in a large number of people.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:50.480
But you know what else
can have serious side effects?

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:51.520
Obesity.

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:54.080
In fact, one potential
side effect of GLP-1 drugs

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:56.080
is that they could be
too effective,

00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:57.983
risking excessive weight loss.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:00.000
Any discussion
of risks versus benefits

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.520
has to take any benefits

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:04.240
of the weight loss itself
into account.

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:06.880
Excess body fat
is a major risk factor

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:08.400
for metabolic diseases,

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.640
involving nearly
every organ in our body,

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:12.320
such as Type II diabetes,

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:14.640
heart disease, stroke,
dementia, liver disease,

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:17.280
sleep apnea,
osteoarthritis, infertility,

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:18.080
several cancers,

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:19.680
including breast cancer
and colon cancer,

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:22.080
even psychiatric disorders.

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:23.920
Consider
the overall health outcomes

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:26.080
of those undergoing
bariatric surgery,

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:28.360
which is not exactly
a benign procedure.

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:30.800
In the United States,
for instance,

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:32.720
hundreds of thousands
go under the knife

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:33.920
to lose weight.

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:35.520
Roux-en-Y gastric bypass

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:37.200
is one of
the most popular techniques

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:39.600
and is thought to be
the "gold standard" method

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:40.960
given its safety record,

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:44.480
with a mortality rate
less 0.5%.

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:46.560
Wait, they’re bragging
about not killing

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:49.680
more than 1 in 200 people
in the operating room?

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:52.560
The surgery
is a major rearrangement

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:54.240
of your digestive tract,

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:56.320
but it can induce
a long-term weight loss

00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:57.840
of about 25%,

00:01:57.840 --> 00:01:59.440
which is similar
to some of the best results

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:01.520
of the new GLP-1 drugs.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:03.920
So, if you only care
about living longer,

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:05.760
might the benefits
of weight loss

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:09.040
outweigh the risks of dying
on the operating table?

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:12.000
Based on a meta-analysis
of millions of patients,

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:14.400
only about 1 in 1,250 people

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.520
appear to be killed
directly by the surgery,

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:19.360
and since the ones
who don’t lose their lives

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:21.520
tend to lose so much weight,

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:23.200
bariatric surgery
has been associated

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:26.400
with a six-year longer lifespan.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:30.080
So, on average,
choosing to go under the knife

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:32.320
may significantly
extend your life,

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:34.160
even after taking into account
the risk

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:36.400
of the operation itself
killing you.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:39.360
But, of course, there’s also
the risk of complications.

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:41.760
Approximately 1 in 4
bariatric surgery patients

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:42.880
experience adverse effects

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:44.720
in the five years
following surgery,

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:46.720
and for 1 in 50,
it’s so bad

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:48.960
that they have to go back
onto the operating table

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:50.720
for further surgery.

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:53.040
That’s one advantage
of the drug approach.

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:55.040
If you experience
some serious side effect,

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:57.680
it may go away
when you stop taking the drug,

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:00.240
whereas if you’ve already
had your stomach cut out,

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:02.240
or your intestines rearranged,

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:05.040
there may be less
that can be done about it.

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:08.160
Here’s a list
of the pros and cons.

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:10.880
Researchers looked at
the impact of bariatric surgery

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:13.440
on more than five dozen
health outcomes.

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:15.280
And although people
who underwent surgery

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:16.880
may be more likely
to kill themselves,

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:18.880
break bones,
and suffer acid reflux,

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:22.320
they also appear
to get less diabetes,

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:23.840
high blood pressure,
and high cholesterol,

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:26.480
and less cancer
and cardiovascular disease.

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:28.560
Here’s how it breaks down.

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:29.280
Just looking at

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:32.160
the statistically
significant associations,

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:34.800
we can see that those
who’ve had bariatric surgery

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:37.920
had a lower risk of dying
from all causes put together,

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:40.160
as well as dying
specifically from diabetes,

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:42.560
cancer,
and cardiovascular disease,

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:44.000
but they are
at an increased risk

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.840
of taking their own lives.

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:47.600
In terms of metabolic outcomes,

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:49.360
lower risks of getting diabetes,

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:50.880
high blood pressure
and high cholesterol.

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:53.600
Lower risks of continuing
to have diabetes,

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:55.040
high blood pressure,
and cholesterol,

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:57.320
and a lower risk
of diabetic complications.

00:03:57.320 --> 00:03:59.040
In terms of getting cancer,

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:00.400
there’s a lower risk
of developing

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:01.280
different types of cancer

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:03.360
and getting
any kind of cancer at all.

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:05.680
A lower risk of all
the cardiovascular diseases

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:06.880
the researchers looked at,

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:09.120
and most
of the digestive diseases

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:11.920
except for reflux
with sleeve gastrectomy,

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:14.000
and higher or lower risk
of kidney stones

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:15.520
depending on procedure,

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:18.480
but it generally seems
to be kidney protective.

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:20.720
For women’s health,
after bariatric surgery,

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:22.320
they had less
urinary incontinence

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:23.920
and polycystic ovary syndrome,

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:26.560
and fewer problems
during pregnancy,

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:28.320
though the outcomes
for infants are mixed,

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:30.880
with more preterm
birth and death.

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:33.760
And finally,
less anxiety and depression,

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:34.960
though more self-harm,

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:36.640
and a lower risk
of being hospitalized

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:38.800
and dying from COVID.

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:43.360
So, generally, the benefits
far outweigh the risks,

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:46.800
but, really, that says less
about the benefits of surgery

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:49.920
and more about the risks
of excess body fat.

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:51.360
With the GLP-1 drugs,

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:52.880
we see
largely similar improvements

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:54.320
in things like
blood sugar control,

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:55.680
blood pressure,
and cholesterol,

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:57.840
and maybe even
similar clinical outcomes,

00:04:57.840 --> 00:04:59.120
like the risk of dying.

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:00.160
If that were the case,

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:02.320
then for most people
with obesity,

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:04.400
like with the bariatric surgery,

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:05.680
the benefits of these new drugs

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:08.880
would be expected
to far exceed the risks.

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:10.800
Yes, there are still issues
with the cost

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:12.720
of these potentially
life-long medications,

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:15.360
and lack of knowledge
of their long-term side effects,

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:16.320
and this, of course,

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:19.040
assumes you’re taking
the actual drug.

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:20.160
Shortages of these pills

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:22.400
have led patients
to compounding pharmacies

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:24.800
that offer versions of the drugs
that have not been approved

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:27.120
by the U.S. Food
and Drug Administration,

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:30.480
which in the past has led
to serious safety issues,

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:33.120
like an epidemic
of fungal meningitis

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:37.360
caused by moldy bottles of drugs
from compounding pharmacies.

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:40.000
751 patients
were ultimately affected,

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:43.040
and more than 60 patients died.

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:44.640
But at least
compounding pharmacies

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:46.640
have some kind of regulation.

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:48.400
Nowadays,
people can get injected

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:51.760
with God knows what
at so-called medical spas

00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:55.120
that may not be under
any form of regulation.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:57.520
People don’t seem
to be paying much attention

00:05:57.520 --> 00:06:00.480
to these FDA warnings.

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:02.320
As an article
in Rolling Stone put it,

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:04.480
"The FDA warned Ozempic users,"

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:07.760
but, "They don’t give a ..."

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:10.000
Yes, these drugs
can improve risk factors,

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:12.640
but the risk-benefit analysis
really depends on

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:15.280
these clinical disease outcomes.

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:18.000
Do people really live longer
on these drugs?

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:19.680
Have less heart attacks?

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:21.200
"Thinner is better,"

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:22.800
is the conventional wisdom
when it comes

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:25.040
to minimizing the risk
of cardiovascular events

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:26.800
like heart attacks and strokes,

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:27.920
but there have been cases

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:29.200
where weight loss medications

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:32.320
actually led to increased
cardiovascular risk

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:34.640
despite significant
reductions in body fat.

00:06:34.640 --> 00:06:36.000
So, we can’t just assume

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:38.320
drug-induced weight loss
will help.

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:41.600
Now, if it’s true
that GLP-1 drugs, like Ozempic,

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:43.520
reduce cardiovascular events,

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:45.840
which are some
of our leading causes of death,

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:48.640
then that benefit
would significantly overwhelm

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:51.040
the risk of almost any amount
of thyroid cancer

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:52.640
these drugs may cause.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:54.800
Let’s look at the data.

00:06:54.800 --> 00:06:56.160
Some major trials have found

00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:59.200
that among high-risk
individuals with diabetes,

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:01.920
risk of cardiovascular events
were significantly lower

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:04.080
among those
randomized to Ozempic

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:06.240
compared to placebo injections,

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:08.240
but other trials did not.

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:10.480
Interesting how
the lack of benefit was spun

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:14.240
by saying, "Hey,
it’s not inferior to placebo."

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:15.600
But that was the main concern,

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:17.760
that Ozempic, like some
other weight loss drugs,

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:20.400
could actually increase
cardiovascular disease.

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:23.680
So, it was considered a relief
that it had no effect.

00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:25.920
Enough evidence
of benefit accrued, though,

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:28.160
that Ozempic
and another GLP-1 drug

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:30.960
were approved
for cardiovascular protection

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:34.480
among individuals
with Type II diabetes.

00:07:34.480 --> 00:07:36.800
Remember, these were
originally prescribed

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:38.160
as diabetes drugs.

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:41.520
So, maybe users reduced
their cardiovascular risk

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:43.440
just by lowering
their blood sugars

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:46.000
rather than
by lowering their weight.

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:49.040
What we want to know is this.

00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:50.560
What is the effect of Ozempic

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:52.640
on cardiovascular outcomes
in obesity

00:07:52.640 --> 00:07:55.440
for people without diabetes?

00:07:55.440 --> 00:07:57.040
And, in patients

00:07:57.040 --> 00:07:59.440
who have preexisting
cardiovascular disease,

00:07:59.440 --> 00:08:01.120
and are overweight or obese,

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:03.040
but do not have diabetes,

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:05.840
those randomized
to weight loss doses of Ozempic

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:07.440
had an overall lower rate

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:09.680
of either having
a cardiovascular event,

00:08:09.680 --> 00:08:10.800
like a heart attack or stroke,

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:13.920
or dying from it,
compared to placebo.

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:15.280
That’s exciting,

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:17.440
but we have to highlight
another caveat, though.

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:18.800
The researchers
just looked at

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:22.720
those with preexisting
cardiovascular disease.

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:24.800
That is an important
limitation of these findings.

00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:26.240
The effects of these
weight-loss drugs

00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:28.240
on the prevention
of cardiovascular events

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:31.120
in those without diagnosed
atherosclerotic disease

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:34.080
have not yet been determined.

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:35.840
Still, a lot
of overweight people

00:08:35.840 --> 00:08:37.040
have a history of heart attack,

00:08:37.040 --> 00:08:38.880
stroke,
or peripheral vascular disease.

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:41.360
So, how big is the benefit?

00:08:41.360 --> 00:08:43.280
Over a period of a few years,

00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:45.440
8% of people
with cardiovascular disease

00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:47.520
suffered another event
on the placebo,

00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:50.640
but only 6.5%
suffered a subsequent event

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:52.080
on the drug.

00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:56.523
Going from 8 to 6.5
is a 20% drop.

00:08:56.560 --> 00:08:58.720
Unfortunately,
many news stories focused on

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:00.960
that 20% relative risk reduction

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:03.040
rather than on
the absolute risk reduction

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:05.120
of 1.5%.

00:09:05.120 --> 00:09:08.560
Yes, 8 to 6.5 is a 20% drop,

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:09.440
but, at the same time,

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:13.520
you’re really only reducing
your absolute risk by 1.5%.

00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:14.160
In other words,

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:16.400
you’d have to treat
67 people with the drug

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:18.640
for a few years
to prevent one heart attack

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:21.280
or stroke
or cardiovascular death.

00:09:21.280 --> 00:09:24.400
That may not sound like much
on an individual scale.

00:09:24.400 --> 00:09:25.600
I mean, what are the odds

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:28.080
you’re going to be
that 1 in 67th person?

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:30.880
But on a population scale,
it’s huge.

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:32.160
In fact, it’s right up there

00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:34.240
with cholesterol-lowering
statin drugs,

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:35.680
which have
an absolute risk reduction

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:38.720
in the same 1.5% ballpark.

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:40.800
So, indeed, in March 2024,

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:42.000
the Food and Drug Administration

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:43.520
approved high-dose Ozempic

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:45.040
for use beyond just weight loss

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:47.680
but also for reducing
cardiovascular risk

00:09:47.680 --> 00:09:52.160
in those with
prior cardiovascular disease.

00:09:52.160 --> 00:09:55.520
So, how do the benefits
and harms stack up?

00:09:55.520 --> 00:09:56.960
In the summer of 2024,

00:09:56.960 --> 00:10:00.000
the first quantitative
benefit-harm balance analysis

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:01.200
was published.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:02.320
The researchers concluded

00:10:02.320 --> 00:10:05.040
that for those achieving
a 10% weight loss,

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:07.040
there’s more than a 90% chance

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:08.720
the benefits outweigh the harms,

00:10:08.720 --> 00:10:11.680
though the opposite was found
for only a 5% weight loss.

00:10:11.680 --> 00:10:13.280
Here’s how they broke it down.

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:16.240
If 1,000 people
go on these GLP-1 drugs,

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:18.800
375 would be expected to lose

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:20.160
at least 10%
of their body weight

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:22.720
with all the ancillary benefits
that would bring.

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:24.640
On the other side
of the equation,

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:27.600
41 people would suffer
from abdominal pain,

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:30.400
57 from hair loss,
8 from gallstones,

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:33.120
118 from constipation,
100 from diarrhea,

00:10:33.120 --> 00:10:36.080
22 from dizziness,
84 from an upset stomach,

00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:39.200
46 from excessive burping,
39 from fatigue,

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:42.240
51 from excessive farting,
13 from headaches,

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:43.680
17 from low blood sugars,

00:10:43.680 --> 00:10:46.000
4 from reactions
at the injection site.

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:49.280
221 would suffer from nausea,
4 from pancreatitis,

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:52.880
43 from upper abdominal pain,
and 110 from vomiting.

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:56.240
Now, of course, the net benefit
versus harm calculation

00:10:56.240 --> 00:10:58.240
would be highly dependent on

00:10:58.240 --> 00:11:01.040
different people’s willingness
to accept different harms.

00:11:01.040 --> 00:11:03.520
Like a bald guy
isn’t going to be concerned

00:11:03.520 --> 00:11:05.200
about hair loss, for example.

00:11:05.200 --> 00:11:07.280
And this also
doesn’t take into account

00:11:07.280 --> 00:11:09.920
the fact that
the benefits peter out.

00:11:09.920 --> 00:11:11.520
Weight loss stalls after a year,

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:13.200
but the harms may continue.

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:14.960
So, once
you’ve already plateaued

00:11:14.960 --> 00:11:16.720
and stop losing weight,

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:18.240
do you keep taking it

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:20.000
even though you get
no further weight-loss benefit

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:24.080
but the potential for harm
continues to accumulate?

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:27.360
We really don’t know about
the long-term harms or benefits

00:11:27.360 --> 00:11:30.640
because some of these drugs
and dosing schedules are so new,

00:11:30.640 --> 00:11:33.600
especially now that the American
Academy of Pediatrics

00:11:33.600 --> 00:11:35.040
has suggested
offering these drugs

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:38.320
for teens and tweens
as young as age 12.

00:11:38.320 --> 00:11:40.640
These drugs work
by acting on the brain,

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:43.040
so, who knows what effect
this could have

00:11:43.040 --> 00:11:44.880
on childhood development
and beyond,

00:11:44.880 --> 00:11:48.240
if they end up taking them
for the rest of their lives.

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:51.280
In the end,
this story is familiar.

00:11:51.280 --> 00:11:53.360
A new class
of antidiabetic agents

00:11:53.360 --> 00:11:55.360
is rushed to market
and widely promoted

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:56.560
in the absence
of any evidence

00:11:56.560 --> 00:11:58.800
of long-term
beneficial outcomes.

00:11:58.800 --> 00:12:00.400
Evidence of harms accumulate,

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:03.200
but it’s vigorously denied
or discounted.

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:06.640
The manufacturers are expected,
quite unrealistically,

00:12:06.640 --> 00:12:09.200
to monitor the safety
of their own products.

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:11.040
We should be thankful
that those responsible

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:12.320
for aircraft safety

00:12:12.320 --> 00:12:14.800
do not operate
under the same assumption.

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:16.480
Although we now
do have evidence

00:12:16.480 --> 00:12:18.880
of at least near-term benefit
over a few years,

00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:21.200
we cannot assume
long-term safety

00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:23.840
until it has been demonstrated.

